Argentina entered the tournament also as one of the favorites to win, and earned their World Cup slot by placing first in [[2026 FIFA World Cup qualification (CONMEBOL)|South American qualifiers]].<ref>{{cite news |last1=Vickery |first1=Tim |last2=Becherano |first2=Lizzy |date=June 14, 2026 |title=Can Argentina really win the World Cup again? What stats and the players say |url=https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/49014778/can-argentina-really-win-world-cup-again-stats-players-say |publisher=ESPN |accessdate=July 15, 2026 |archive-date=July 16, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260716025919/https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/49014778/can-argentina-really-win-world-cup-again-stats-players-say |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Rey |first1=Debora |last2=Savarese |first2=Mauricio |date=March 25, 2025 |title=Argentina secures a World Cup spot and then celebrates it with a 4–1 victory over archrival Brazil |url=https://apnews.com/article/argentina-world-cup-brazil-messi-6088e7977b166d279223c8f7176066fd |work=Associated Press News |access-date=July 17, 2026 |archive-date=April 25, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260425061750/https://apnews.com/article/argentina-world-cup-brazil-messi-6088e7977b166d279223c8f7176066fd |url-status=live }}</ref> They were drawn into [[2026 FIFA World Cup Group J|Group J]], alongside [[Algeria national football team|Algeria]], [[Austria national football team|Austria]], and [[Jordan national football team|Jordan]].<ref>{{cite news |last=Millar |first=Colin |date=December 5, 2025 |title=Argentina drawn in 2026 World Cup Group J: What to know about Algeria, Austria, Jordan |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/6854719/2025/12/05/world-cup-draw-argentina-group-schedule-fixtures/ |work=The Athletic |url-access=subscription |accessdate=July 17, 2026 |archive-date=December 5, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251205191011/https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/6854719/2025/12/05/world-cup-draw-argentina-group-schedule-fixtures/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Their first match was against Algeria on June 16 at [[Arrowhead Stadium]] in [[Kansas City]], near Argentina's base camp.<ref>{{cite news |last=Green |first=PJ |date=May 31, 2026 |title=See fans cheer Argentina soccer team arriving in Kansas City for 2026 World Cup |url=https://www.kansascity.com/sports/fifa-world-cup/article315956000.html |work=[[The Kansas City Star]] |accessdate=July 17, 2026}}</ref> Argentina won 3–0 through a [[List of FIFA World Cup hat-tricks|hat trick]] by [[Lionel Messi]], who equaled the record for [[List of FIFA World Cup top goalscorers|most World Cup goals]].<ref>{{cite news |last=MacDonald |first=Keifer |title=Argentina 3–0 Algeria: Lionel Messi scores his first World Cup hat trick to equal Miroslav Klose record |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/ckg78g6pnyzt |work=BBC Sport |accessdate=July 15, 2026 |archive-date=July 18, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260718090050/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/ckg78g6pnyzt |url-status=live }}</ref> In their second match against Austria on June 22 at AT&T Stadium near Dallas, Messi scored twice and the team won 2–0.<ref>{{cite news |last=Ames |first=Nick |date=June 22, 2026 |title=Irrepressible Messi breaks World Cup scoring record as Argentina beat Austria |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/jun/22/argentina-austria-world-cup-group-j-match-report |work=The Guardian |accessdate=July 17, 2026}}</ref> Argentina finished atop the group with nine points after a 3–1 win against World Cup debutants Jordan on June 27 in Atlanta. [[Giovani Lo Celso]] scored the opening goal in the 19th minute to give Argentina the lead, which was followed by a penalty that was converted by [[Lautaro Martínez]]. [[Musa Al-Taamari]] scored for Jordan to break the shutout, but Messi entered the match as a substitute and scored from a free kick in the 80th minute.<ref>{{cite news |last=Drury |first=Sam |date=June 28, 2026 |title=Jordan 1–3 Argentina: Lionel Messi comes on to score sixth goal of World Cup 2026 |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/c20ye67xgykt |work=BBC Sport |accessdate=July 17, 2026 |archive-date=July 16, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260716020659/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/c20ye67xgykt |url-status=live }}</ref>

As group winners, Argentina played Group H runners-up Cape Verde in the round of 32 on July 3 at [[Hard Rock Stadium]] near [[Miami]]. Messi opened the scoring in the 29th minute from close range, but a run and finish by [[Deroy Duarte]] allowed Cape Verde to equalize in the second half. The match remained tied and went to [[extra time (association football)|extra time]], where [[Lisandro Martínez]] put Argentina in the lead within two minutes. [[Sidny Lopes Cabral]] equalized for Cape Verde with a curling shot that beat [[Emiliano Martínez]] in the 103rd minute, but was followed by an [[own goal]] off the arm of [[Diney Borges]] on a corner kick to give Argentina a 3–2 victory.<ref>{{cite news |last=Ronay |first=Barney |date=July 3, 2026 |title=Cape Verde threaten shock for the ages before Argentina break hearts in World Cup classic |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/jul/04/argentina-cape-verde-world-cup-2026-last-32-match-report |work=The Guardian |accessdate=July 17, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Coates |first=Charlotte |date=July 3, 2026 |title=Argentina 3–2 Cape Verde (AET): Messi through as holders survive scare to reach World Cup last 16 |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/cz75y0v8qrjt |work=BBC Sport |accessdate=July 17, 2026 |archive-date=July 15, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260715200548/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/cz75y0v8qrjt |url-status=live }}</ref> In the round of 16 on July 7, Argentina faced [[Egypt national football team|Egypt]] in Atlanta and conceded two goals to [[Yasser Ibrahim]] and [[Mostafa Ziko]]. Messi had an earlier penalty kick saved, but provided an assist to [[Cristian Romero]]'s header before scoring himself to tie the match in the 83rd minute.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Garsd |first1=Jasmine |last2=Lewis |first2=Russell |date=July 7, 2026 |title=Reigning champion Argentina escapes with remarkable World Cup victory over Egypt |url=https://www.npr.org/2026/07/07/nx-s1-5884872/2026-world-cup-fifa-argentina-egypt-round-of-16 |publisher=NPR |accessdate=July 17, 2026 |archive-date=July 8, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260708170632/https://www.npr.org/2026/07/07/nx-s1-5884872/2026-world-cup-fifa-argentina-egypt-round-of-16 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name="BBC-EGY">{{cite news |last=Howarth |first=Matthew |date=July 7, 2026 |title=World Cup 2026 results: Argentina 3–2 Egypt as Lionel Messi scores after having penalty saved |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/cdr4m2122lgt |work=BBC Sport |accessdate=July 17, 2026 |archive-date=July 10, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260710205208/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/cdr4m2122lgt |url-status=live }}</ref> Argentina won 3–2 with a header from [[Enzo Fernández]] in the second minute of stoppage time amid controversy over a disallowed goal and penalty by the referee.<ref name="BBC-EGY"/><ref>{{cite news |last1=Chutel |first1=Lynsey |last2=Khaled |first2=Rania |date=July 8, 2026 |title=Heartbreak and Anger in Egypt Over a Stinging World Cup Loss to Argentina |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/08/world/africa/egypt-argentina-goal-referee-conspiracy.html |work=The New York Times |url-access=subscription |accessdate=July 17, 2026}}</ref>

[[File:P20260719DT-0633 President Donald J. Trump and First Lady Melania Trump attend the FIFA World Cup Final.jpg|thumb|left|upright=0.88|Argentina's starting lineup during the final.]]
The team returned to Kansas City for their quarterfinal match against [[Switzerland national football team|Switzerland]] on July 11, played in hot and humid conditions. [[Alexis Mac Allister]] scored with a header in the 10th minute to give Argentina the lead, but the match was tied in the 67th minute by [[Dan Ndoye]].<ref name="ABC-SUI">{{cite news |last=Skretta |first=Dave |date=July 11, 2026 |title=Argentina beats Switzerland 3–1 in extra time, advancing to World Cup semifinals |url=https://abcnews.com/Sports/wireStory/argentina-lineup-unchanged-messi-alongside-alvarez-world-cup-134686135 |work=ABC News |agency=Associated Press |accessdate=July 17, 2026 |archive-date=July 14, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260714104253/https://abcnews.com/Sports/wireStory/argentina-lineup-unchanged-messi-alongside-alvarez-world-cup-134686135 |url-status=live }}</ref> Switzerland lost [[Breel Embolo]] five minutes later to a [[red card (association football)|red card]] after the [[video assistant referee]] determined there was a case of mistaken identity for another foul, which resulted in a second [[yellow card (association football)|yellow card]]. Argentina eventually won 3–1 in extra time through a long-distance strike by [[Julián Alvarez]] and a rebound from Lautaro Martínez.<ref name="ABC-SUI"/><ref>{{cite news |last=Ames |first=Nick |date=July 11, 2026 |title=Julián Álvarez's extra-time stunner sinks 10-man Switzerland to send Argentina into semi-finals |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/jul/12/switzerland-argentina-world-cup-quarter-final-match-report |work=The Guardian |accessdate=July 17, 2026}}</ref> Argentina advanced to the semifinal on July 15 in Atlanta, where they faced [[England national football team|England]], a [[Argentina–England football rivalry|longtime rival]] in the World Cup.<ref>{{cite news |last=Alcoba |first=Natalie |date=July 15, 2026 |title=Old rivals, new battle: Argentina and England clash in World Cup Semifinal |url=https://www.npr.org/2026/07/15/nx-s1-5893686/old-rivals-new-battle-argentina-and-england-clash-in-world-cup-semi-final |publisher=NPR |accessdate=July 17, 2026}}</ref> After [[Anthony Gordon (footballer)|Anthony Gordon]] goal in the 55th minute gave England the lead, head coach [[Thomas Tuchel]] switched to a five-defender formation with several substitutions.<ref name="Guardian-ENG">{{cite news |last=Hytner |first=David |date=July 15, 2026 |title=Argentina's late double breaks England hearts in dramatic World Cup semi-final |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/jul/15/england-argentina-world-cup-semi-final-match-report |work=The Guardian |accessdate=July 17, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Hamilton |first=Tom |date=July 16, 2026 |title=Tuchel's retreat set up England's World Cup exit as Argentina smelled blood |url=https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/49373334/tuchel-retreat-set-england-world-cup-exit-argentina-smelt-blood |publisher=ESPN |accessdate=July 17, 2026 |archive-date=July 16, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260716083957/https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/49373334/tuchel-retreat-set-england-world-cup-exit-argentina-smelt-blood |url-status=live }}</ref> Messi provided assists for the equalizer in the 86th minute by Enzo Fernández and Lautaro Martínez's winning header in the second minute of stoppage time. Argentina won 2–1 to reach their second consecutive World Cup final.<ref name="Guardian-ENG"/>

==Entertainment==

===Closing ceremony===
[[File:FIFAAH-06756 President Donald J. Trump and First Lady Melania Trump attend the FIFA World Cup Final.jpg|210x210px|thumb|Artistic performance during the closing ceremony]]

A closing ceremony for the World Cup began at 1:40 p.m. [[Eastern Time Zone|Eastern Daylight Time]] ([[UTC−4]]), eighty minutes before the scheduled kickoff. [[IShowSpeed]] performed his World Cup-themed song "[[World Cup (Champions)|Champions]]", while headliner [[Post Malone]] and rapper [[Swae Lee]] sang "[[Sunflower (Post Malone and Swae Lee song)|Sunflower]]". Afterwards, [[Jennifer Hudson]] sang "[[The Star-Spangled Banner]]", the national anthem of the United States, with Robbie Williams, [[Nicole Scherzinger]] and [[Laura Pausini]] then performing the song "Desire". [[Mario Kempes]] and [[Andrés Iniesta|Andres Iniesta]], two respective members of Argentina's and Spain's winning teams in 1978 and 2010, unveiled the [[FIFA World Cup Trophy]].<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Chan |first=Anna |date=July 14, 2026 |title=World Cup Closing Ceremony to Feature Jennifer Hudson, Nicole Scherzinger & More |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/world-cup-closing-ceremony-jennifer-hudson-nicole-scherzinger-1236293796/ |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |access-date=July 14, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260715064512/https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/world-cup-closing-ceremony-jennifer-hudson-nicole-scherzinger-1236293796/ |archive-date=July 15, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=July 19, 2026 |title=History made by stunning closing ceremony and Halftime Show |url=https://www.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/worldcup/canadamexicousa2026/articles/best-of-closing-ceremony-halftime-show |access-date=July 24, 2026 |website=FIFA}}</ref>[[File:FIFAAH-06520 President Donald J. Trump and First Lady Melania Trump attend the FIFA World Cup Final.jpg|thumb|Color smoke representing the national flags of Spain and Argentina drifts across MetLife Stadium's pitch, minutes before kickoff.|210x210px]][[Marcha Real|Spain's national anthem]] was performed by the Spanish brass quintet {{ill|Spanish Brass|es}}, while Argentine singer [[María Becerra]] sang [[Argentine National Anthem|Argentina's national anthem]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Who's singing Argentina's national anthem before the 2026 World Cup Final vs. Spain today? |url=https://bolavip.com/en/world-cup/whos-singing-argentinas-national-anthem-before-the-2026-world-cup-final-vs-spain |access-date=July 20, 2026 |agency=Bolavip USA |date=July 19, 2026 |archive-date=July 19, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260719190159/https://bolavip.com/en/world-cup/whos-singing-argentinas-national-anthem-before-the-2026-world-cup-final-vs-spain |url-status=live }}</ref>

===Halftime show===
{{main|2026 FIFA World Cup final halftime show}}
[[File:P20260719DT-1056 President Donald J. Trump and First Lady Melania Trump attend the FIFA World Cup Final.jpg|200px|thumb|right|[[Madonna]] and the Brazilian player [[Ronaldo (Brazilian footballer)|Ronaldo]] during the halftime show]]

The 2026 final was the first to feature a [[halftime show]], similar to those in the NFL's [[Super Bowl]]. The show was announced by FIFA on November 28, 2024, with [[Global Citizen (organization)|Global Citizen]] listed as the co-producer.<ref>{{cite news |last=Willman |first=Chris |date=September 28, 2024 |url=https://variety.com/2024/music/news/world-cup-final-halftime-show-global-citizen-produce-fifa-starting-2026-1236158976/ |title=Global Citizen to Produce Halftime Show for FIFA World Cup Final, Starting in 2026 |access-date=June 28, 2026 |work=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240928223758/https://variety.com/2024/music/news/world-cup-final-halftime-show-global-citizen-produce-fifa-starting-2026-1236158976/ |archive-date=September 28, 2024}}</ref> It was curated by [[Chris Martin]] of [[Coldplay]].<ref>{{cite news |last=Willman |first=Chris |date=March 5, 2025 |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/cge1q41np7go |title=Coldplay to pick 2026 World Cup final half-time acts |access-date=June 28, 2026 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250305131545/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/cge1q41np7go |archive-date=March 5, 2025}}</ref> The performance also aimed to raise $100&nbsp;million for the FIFA Global Citizen Education Fund.<ref name="BBC-Halftime">{{cite news |last=McKenna |first=Lorraine |date=May 14, 2026 |title=Madonna, Shakira & BTS to headline World Cup show |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/c5yrl54561do |access-date=May 14, 2026 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260514111629/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/c5yrl54561do |archive-date=May 14, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> The show was headlined by [[Madonna]], [[Shakira]], [[Justin Bieber]] and [[BTS]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Saad |first=Nardine |date=July 8, 2026 |title=Justin Bieber joins Madonna, Shakira and BTS for Fifa World Cup final half-time show |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c1wyx7g9e1do |access-date=July 9, 2026 |publisher=[[BBC]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260709041302/https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c1wyx7g9e1do |archive-date=July 9, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> It also included guest performances by [[Gustavo Dudamel]], [[New York Philharmonic]], [[Simón Bolívar Symphony Orchestra]], [[Bijan Mortazavi]], [[Electric Mayhem]], [[Burna Boy]], [[Ghetto Kids]], [[The Muppets]], [[Emmanuel Kelly]] and [[PS22 Chorus]], as well as guest appearances by [[Jason Sudeikis]] and [[Brendan Hunt]] as their characters from the television series ''[[Ted Lasso]]''.<ref>{{cite news |last=Hustin |first=Caitlin |title=Madonna, Justin Bieber, BTS, Shakira Headline Jam-Packed First-Ever FIFA World Cup Final Halftime Show |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/music/music-news/fifa-world-cup-halftime-madonna-justin-bieber-bts-shakira-1236651689/ |magazine=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |date=July 19, 2026 |access-date=July 19, 2026 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260719204241/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/music/music-news/fifa-world-cup-halftime-madonna-justin-bieber-bts-shakira-1236651689/ |archive-date=July 19, 2026 }}</ref>

The halftime show was criticized by commentators and fans as being too [[commercialization|commercialized]] and an unwanted [[Americanization]] of the match.<ref>{{cite news |last=Church |first=Ben |date=May 15, 2026 |url=https://edition.cnn.com/2026/05/15/sport/world-cup-halftime-show-reaction |title=Why some purists can't stand the idea of a World Cup halftime show |publisher=CNN |access-date=June 26, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260516130825/https://edition.cnn.com/2026/05/15/sport/world-cup-halftime-show-reaction |archive-date=May 16, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Guardian-Halftime">{{cite news |last=Hughes |first=Matt |date=June 10, 2026 |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/jun/10/tv-rights-holders-frustrated-over-world-cup-final-half-time-show-delay |title=TV rights holders frustrated over World Cup final half-time show delay |work=[[The Guardian]] |access-date=June 26, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260610181725/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/jun/10/tv-rights-holders-frustrated-over-world-cup-final-half-time-show-delay |archive-date=June 10, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> The halftime break lasted 27 minutes and 22 seconds,<ref>{{cite news |last=Halpert |first=Madeline |date=July 19, 2026 |title=Shakira, Madonna, Justin Bieber and BTS perform at colourful World Cup half-time show |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/clyxjl0wkl7o |access-date=July 24, 2026 |publisher=[[BBC]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260721021010/https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/clyxjl0wkl7o |archive-date=July 21, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> which broke the [[International Football Association Board|IFAB]] [[Laws of the Game (association football)|Laws of the Game]] which state that the halftime break cannot exceed 15 minutes.<ref name="Guardian-Halftime"/><ref>{{cite news |last1=Sheldon |first1=Dan |last2=Crafton |first2=Adam |date=July 14, 2026 |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/7445380/2026/07/14/world-cup-half-time-length-fifa/ |title=FIFA targeting 20-minute break for World Cup half-time |access-date=July 15, 2026 |work=[[The Athletic]] |url-access=subscription |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260714194433/https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/7445380/2026/07/14/world-cup-half-time-length-fifa/ |archive-date=July 14, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Marcotti |first=Gabriele |author-link=Gabriele Marcotti |date=March 8, 2025 |url=https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/44164198/fifa-world-cup-half-show-gianni-infantino-only-15-minutes-super-bowl |title=FIFA can have a World Cup halftime show... within 15 minutes |access-date=June 26, 2026 |publisher=ESPN |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260514115407/https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/44164198/fifa-world-cup-half-show-gianni-infantino-only-15-minutes-super-bowl |archive-date=May 14, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> On the [[BBC]] live broadcast of the match, [[Wayne Rooney]] said of the halftime show, "It was crap."<ref>{{cite news |last1=Unwin |first1=Will |title='It was crap': Wayne Rooney's candour helps BBC in World Cup final TV battle |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/jul/19/world-cup-2026-final-tv-review-bbc-itv-wayne-rooney |access-date=July 20, 2026 |work=[[The Guardian]] |date=July 19, 2026 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260721034138/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/jul/19/world-cup-2026-final-tv-review-bbc-itv-wayne-rooney |archive-date=July 21, 2026}}</ref>

==Pre-match==
On July 16, 2026, [[Slavko Vinčić]], from Slovenia, was named as the [[Referee (association football)|referee]] of the final, together with fellow Slovenes Tomaž Klančnik and Andraž Kovačič as [[Assistant referee (association football)#Assistant referee|assistant referees]] and  [[Adham Makhadmeh]] and Mohammad Al-Kalaf from Jordan as the fourth [[Assistant referee (association football)#Fourth official|official]] and [[Assistant referee (association football)#Fifth official and reserve assistant referee|reserve assistant referee]]. The VAR team consisted of [[Bastian Dankert]], [[Nicolás Gallo (referee)|Nicolas Gallo]], and [[Khamis Al-Marri|Khamis Al-Marri.]] [[Tatiana Guzmán|Tatiana Guzman]] and Guillermo Pacheco served as standby VARs.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Singh |first=Pragjyoti |date=July 19, 2026 |title=Who Is the Referee In Spain vs. Argentina World Cup Final Match? |url=https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/referee-spain-vs-argentina-world-184500511.html |access-date=July 21, 2026 |website=Yahoo Sports |language=en-US}}</ref> Earlier in the tournament, Vinčić officiated the Brazil–Morocco and Jordan–Algeria matches in the group stage and the Mexico–Ecuador match in the round of 32.<ref name="ESPN-Referee2">{{cite news |date=July 17, 2026|title=Who is Slavko Vincic? Spain vs. Argentina referee for World Cup final drew Real Madrid backlash, Jose Mourinho praise|url=https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/49382615/who-slavko-vincic-spain-vs-argentina-referee-world-cup-final-real-madrid-jose-mourinho-jude-bellingham|publisher=ESPN|accessdate=July 17, 2026}}</ref><ref name=":02">{{cite press release |date=July 16, 2026|title=Slovenian Slavko Vinčić to take charge of FIFA World Cup 2026 final|url=https://inside.fifa.com/refereeing/news/slavko-vincic-world-cup-2026-final-referee-spain-argentina|publisher=FIFA|accessdate=July 17, 2026|archive-date=July 17, 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260717063616/https://inside.fifa.com/refereeing/news/slavko-vincic-world-cup-2026-final-referee-spain-argentina|url-status=live}}</ref> He had previously taken charge of the [[2022 UEFA Europa League final]] and [[2024 UEFA Champions League final]]. He also was one of the referees at the [[UEFA Euro 2020]], [[2022 FIFA World Cup|2022 World Cup]], [[UEFA Euro 2024]], and [[2025 FIFA Club World Cup]]. He became the first Slovenian to referee a World Cup final.<ref name=":02" />

===Dignitaries in attendance===
US president [[Donald Trump]] attended the match and later presented the trophy to the winning team, which received 30 [[championship ring]]s similar to those used by North American sports leagues.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Rampling |first1=Ali |last2=Tansley |first2=Eduardo |date=July 17, 2026 |title=World Cup winners to be presented with championship rings in tournament first |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/7451605/2026/07/17/world-cup-winners-championship-rings/ |work=The Athletic |url-access=subscription |accessdate=July 17, 2026}}</ref> King of Spain [[Felipe VI]], Queen [[Queen Letizia of Spain|Letizia]], with [[Leonor, Princess of Asturias]], [[Infanta Sofía]] and Spanish prime minister [[Pedro Sánchez]] attended the match to watch their country's national team in the final. Citing his superstitious beliefs, Argentine president [[Javier Milei]] declined to attend.<ref>{{cite news |date=July 17, 2026 |title=Spanish royals and PM to attend WCup final but not Argentina leader |url=https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/spanish-royals-pm-attend-wcup-110540267.html |work=Yahoo Sports |agency=[[Deutsche Presse-Agentur]] |accessdate=July 17, 2026 |archive-date=July 18, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260718085050/https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/spanish-royals-pm-attend-wcup-110540267.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date=July 16, 2026 |title=Superstitious Argentine president Milei won't attend World Cup final |url=https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/49380261/argentina-president-javier-milei-attend-2026-world-cup-final |publisher=ESPN |agency=Associated Press |accessdate=July 17, 2026 |archive-date=July 17, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260717025511/https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/49380261/argentina-president-javier-milei-attend-2026-world-cup-final |url-status=live }}</ref> Mexican president [[Claudia Sheinbaum]] and Canadian prime minister [[Mark Carney]], representing the two other co-hosts, attended the final after being invited by Trump.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Orozco |first1=Jose |last2=Hilarie |first2=Valentine |date=July 17, 2026 |title=Sheinbaum, Carney to Watch World Cup Final With Trump |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-07-18/sheinbaum-carney-to-watch-world-cup-final-with-trump |work=[[Bloomberg News]] |url-access=subscription |accessdate=July 18, 2026}}</ref> 

Although [[UEFA]] President [[Aleksander Čeferin]] attended the tournament's June 11, [[2026 FIFA World Cup opening ceremonies|opening match in Mexico City]], he boycotted the final after a [[2026 Trump–FIFA red card controversy|dispute with FIFA over a suspended disciplinary ban]] issued to [[United States men's national soccer team|United States]] player [[Folarin Balogun]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Rumsby |first=Ben |date=July 20, 2026 |title=Uefa president boycotts World Cup final after Fifa's role in Balogun saga |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/football/2026/07/20/uefa-president-boycotts-world-cup-final/ |access-date=July 20, 2026 |work=[[The Telegraph]] (UK)}}</ref> Čeferin, representing the European confederation of which Spain is a member, criticized FIFA's decision to defer Balogun's automatic suspension after he received a red card during a round of 32 match against [[Bosnia and Herzegovina national football team|Bosnia and Herzegovina]], which the United States won 2–0.<ref>{{Cite news |date=July 20, 2026 |title=Aleksander Ceferin boycotts World Cup final after Folarin Balogun scandal |url=https://www.thetimes.com/sport/football/world-cup/article/aleksander-ceferin-boycott-world-cup-final-folarin-balogun-ts6dfjk87 |work=[[The Times]]}}</ref> In contrast, [[CONMEBOL]] President [[Alejandro Domínguez (football executive)|Alejandro Domínguez]] attended the final to support Argentina alongside [[Argentine Football Association]] (AFA) President [[Claudio Tapia]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=July 20, 2026 |title=FIFA World Cup 2026: CONMEBOL chief Alejandro Dominguez meets US Secretary of State Marco Rubio during Argentina vs Spain final |url=https://www.tribuneindia.com/news/afa-president/fifa-world-cup-2026-conmebol-chief-alejandro-dominguez-meets-us-secretary-of-state-marco-rubio-during-argentina-vs-spain-final |work=[[The Tribune (India)]]}}</ref> Rafael Louzán, President of the [[Royal Spanish Football Federation]] (RFEF), also attended the match.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Vertelney |first=Seth |date=July 19, 2026 |title=Who is sitting with President Donald Trump at World Cup final? |url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/soccer/worldcup/2026/07/19/donald-trump-world-cup-final-suite-dignataries/90974782007/ |access-date=July 20, 2026 |work=[[USA Today]]}}</ref>

==Match==
===Summary===
====First half====
Argentina kicked off the match at 3:06&nbsp;p.m. [[Eastern Time Zone|EDT]] (7:06&nbsp;p.m. [[Coordinated Universal Time|UTC]]) in temperatures of {{convert|80|°F|°C|abbr=on}} with 40% [[humidity]], in front of a crowd of 80,663. The weather at [[Teterboro Airport]], {{convert|4.4|mi|km|abbr=on}} from the stadium,{{efn|Distance measured using Google Maps distance calculator, between Teterboro Airport, coordinates {{Coord|40.8501|N|74.0608|W}} and MetLife Stadium, coordinates {{Coord|40.8135|N|74.0743|W}}<ref>{{Google maps |url=https://www.google.com/maps/place/Teterboro+Airport/@40.858332,-74.0641041,17z |access-date=July 19, 2026 |title=Teterboro Airport}}</ref><ref>{{Google maps |url=https://www.google.com/maps/place/New+York+New+Jersey+Stadium/@40.8135064,-74.0770319,17z |access-date=July 19, 2026 |title=New York New Jersey Stadium}}</ref>}} was recorded as fair before kick-off.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Teterboro, NJ Weather History – July 19, 2026|url=https://www.wunderground.com/history/daily/us/nj/teterboro/KTEB/date/2026-7-19|url-status=|access-date=July 19, 2026|website=[[The Weather Company]]|date=July 19, 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260720194130/https://www.wunderground.com/history/daily/us/nj/teterboro/KTEB/date/2026-7-19|archive-date=July 20, 2026}}</ref> Spain had a chance five minutes in the game when [[Lamine Yamal]] passed the ball to [[Dani Olmo]], who returned it back to him. Yamal took the shot, which deflected off Lisandro Martinez's foot, and Argentina's goalkeeper [[Emiliano Martínez]], who moved toward his right, aligned his foot to save it. Then, Spain's goalkeeper [[Unai Simón|Unai Simon]] ran 40 yards from goal to kick the ball away from [[Lionel Messi]], which lands toward Julián Alvarez, who struggles to control it. On fourteen minutes, [[Alexis Mac Allister]] fouled Dani Olmo during a tackle, in which the referee denied giving a yellow card. Two minutes later, Yamal hit a curl shot toward the goal, but the ball landed softly in Martínez's hands. On 39 minutes, [[Mikel Oyarzabal]] hit a 20-yard (18 m) low shot from a long-range effort, which was saved by Martínez once again. On 41 minutes, [[Lisandro Martínez|Lisandro Martinez]] was booked for a foul on Oyarzabal. After this play, Argentina was forced to make a substitution when Lisandro Martínez was injured and was unable to continue; he was replaced by [[Nicolás Otamendi]] in the 44th minute.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Smyth |first=Rob |date=July 20, 2026 |title=Spain beat Argentina 1–0 after extra time to win the 2026 World Cup – as it happened |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/live/2026/jul/19/spain-v-argentina-world-cup-2026-final-live-updates |access-date=July 20, 2026 |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref><ref name="MTresumen" />

====Second half====
[[File:P20260719DT-1478 President Donald J. Trump and First Lady Melania Trump attend the FIFA World Cup Final.jpg|left|thumb|Scenes during the game]]
At the start of the second half, Spain capitalized on an Argentine buildup error, with the ball falling to [[Alex Baena]], whose shot was saved by Martínez just one minute in, in the 46th. Spain continued to press, and in the 53rd minute, [[Fabián Ruiz]] tried a collective play with Oyarzabal in search of a chance, which did not materialize. A minute later, [[Dani Olmo]] attempted a cross looking for Cucurella, but [[Gonzalo Montiel]] intervened to prevent the ball from reaching him. The clearest chance in the second half came in the 66th minute, when Yamal drove down the right flank to the byline and delivered a cross that [[Ferran Torres]] met with a header, but Martínez held onto it.<ref name="MTresumen">{{Cite news |last=Figueroa |first=Juan Manuel |date=July 19, 2026 |title=¡Furia Roja! España destronó a Messi y a Argentina y es Campeón del Mundial 2026 |url=https://www.mediotiempo.com/futbol/copa-mundial/resumen-partido-espana-vs-argentina-1-0-final-mundial-2026 |work=Mediotiempo |language=es|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260719224932/https://www.mediotiempo.com/futbol/copa-mundial/resumen-partido-espana-vs-argentina-1-0-final-mundial-2026|archive-date=July 19, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref>

The closing minutes of the second half were dominated by Spain, with more crucial saves from Martínez. In the 76th minute, he denied a shot from [[Pedri]], and a minute later he did the same to stop an effort from [[Pau Cubarsí]]. In the 80th minute, [[Nico Williams]] got to the byline and sent in a cross that [[Aymeric Laporte]] rose to meet with a header, only for it to end up safely in Martínez's hands.<ref name="MTresumen" />

Argentina had their first real chance of the match in the 3rd minute of added time, when [[Giuliano Simeone]] hit a low cross from the right, but [[Unai Simón]] intercepted the ball with ease. On the resulting counterattack, Williams carried the ball for 30 meters before taking a powerful shot from the edge of the box, which was also saved by Martínez.<ref name="MTresumen" /> A few seconds later, Argentina lost one player after [[Enzo Fernández]] was sent off for a second yellow card, when his attempt to win a loose ball resulted in a reckless challenge against Cubarsí.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Corcuera |first1=Álvaro |last2=Pineda |first2=Rafael |last3=Benítez |first3=J. M. |last4=Muñoz |first4=Mikel |date=July 19, 2026 |title=Así te hemos contado la victoria de España en la final del Mundial ante Argentina para proclamarse campeona |url=https://elpais.com/deportes/mundial-futbol/2026-07-19/espana-argentina-en-directo-la-final-del-mundial-en-vivo.html |work=[[El País]] |language=es}}</ref>

In the final seconds of regular time, Yamal struck a free kick that Martínez managed to deflect away, sending the match into [[extra time]].<ref name="MTresumen" /> With the expiration of regular time, Argentina became the first team to fail to register a shot during the 90 minutes of a World Cup final.<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Lopesino |first1=Juan |last2=Nelson |first2=David |date=July 19, 2026 |title=Argentina's first 90 minutes against Spain: 0.00 xG and no shots on target |url=https://en.as.com/soccer/world-cup/argentinas-first-90-minutes-against-spain-000-xg-and-no-shots-on-target-f202607-n/ |access-date=July 20, 2026 |website=AS USA |language=en-us}}</ref>

====Extra time====
[[File:Ferran Torres France v Spain 7.24.26-261.jpg|thumb|Ferran Torres, the match's sole goalscorer]]
In the 93rd minute, Williams was not able to head a Pedri cross with enough power, and Martínez dove to his right to make the save.<ref name=":2">{{Cite news |last=Bencid |first=Abraham |date=July 19, 2026 |title=España vs Argentina: resumen, goles en video y resultado de la gran final del Mundial 2026 |url=https://www.clarosports.com/futbol/mundial-2026/espana-vs-argentina-en-vivo-la-final-del-mundial-2026-resultado-y-goles-del-partido-messi-vs-lamine-yamal-hoy-19-de-julio/ |work=[[Claro Sports]] |language=Spanish|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260720234210/https://www.clarosports.com/futbol/mundial-2026/espana-vs-argentina-en-vivo-la-final-del-mundial-2026-resultado-y-goles-del-partido-messi-vs-lamine-yamal-hoy-19-de-julio/|archive-date=July 20, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> Three minutes later, Williams appeared to score, after the ball fell to him following a play done by Merino, but the goal was disallowed because Merino had stepped on Otamendi's foot. Merino then headed a chance wide of Martínez's goal in the 102nd minute. At the start of the second period of extra time, Torres received a ball headed down back by Williams, and struck it powerfully with his left foot from close range to beat Martínez, putting Spain in the lead, 1–0.<ref name="MTresumen" /><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/cgk4ymn3n72t|title= Spain 1 Argentina 0 (AET)|date=July 19, 2026|work=BBC Sport|accessdate=July 22, 2026}}</ref>

After the goal, Argentina began to press in search of an equalizer, which led to counterattacking chances. In the 113th minute, Torres went in front of goal against Martínez and appeared to score his second goal, but it was ruled out for offside. Two minutes later, Messi attempted to catch Simón off guard with a cross from the attacking third that drifted toward the Spanish goal, passing over the crossbar. In the 116th minute, Williams created another opportunity and found himself in a favorable position inside Argentina's box after outrunning [[Nahuel Molina]], but was unable to connect with the ball to shoot or find a teammate to extend Spain's lead. In the 117th minute, Messi's shot from the edge of the box, Argentina's first of the match, struck Merino in the face as the midfielder blocked it, leaving him down on the pitch as the match entered its final minutes.<ref name=":2"/><ref>{{cite web |author= [[The Athletic]]|date= July 19, 2026|title= Lionel Messi had Argentina's first shot of the World Cup final after 116 minutes. It was blocked by the head of Mikel Merino.|url= https://x.com/TheAthleticFC/status/2078978440087409066|website= [[X (social network)]]|access-date=July 20, 2026}}</ref>

In the 120th minute, Argentina's final buildup came from a Simeone pass toward [[Marcos Senesi]] in the box, but Cubarsí cleared the danger for a corner.<ref>{{cite web|last= Cervelló Herrero |first= Laia |date=July 20, 2026 |title= Pau Cubarsi, the World Cup's best youngster who plays like a veteran but looks like an angel |url= https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/7458228/2026/07/20/pau-cubarsi-world-cup-young-player-barcelona/ |website= [[The New York Times]]|access-date = July 20, 2026}}</ref> The resulting corner kick led to a scramble inside the goal area, with the Spanish defense kicking the ball out of bounds. The next corner was deflected by [[Nicolás Tagliafico]] on the near post and fell to Simeone's feet, but his desperate attempt from close to the penalty spot went well over the bar.<ref>{{cite web |last= Zavala|first= Jaime|date= July 20, 2026|title= Simeone, villano en la final argentina: falló un gol y en España optó por subirse las calcetas |url= https://www.canal9.cl/episodios/2026/07/20/simeone-el-villano-de-final-en-argentina-erro-gol-y-prefirio-subirse-las-calcetas-en-tanto-de-espana|website= Canal 9 Bío Bío Televisión|access-date= July 20, 2026}}</ref> In the final minutes, Spain kept possession away from their own goal, while a long free kick from Martínez was comfortably dealt with by the Spanish defense before the final whistle confirmed Spain's title.<ref name=":2" />

