==Post-match==
[[File:P20260719DT-1699 President Donald J. Trump and First Lady Melania Trump attend the FIFA World Cup Final.jpg|thumb|Spain's players celebrating after the final whistle, as Lionel Messi looks on.]]

Following the match, Yamal and Messi embraced and exchanged words, a moment described by FIFA and several media outlets as symbolic of a generational transition in football, with Messi approaching the end of an illustrious career and Yamal, regarded as one of the sport's most promising talents, at the start of his.<ref name="2007photo">{{Cite news |date=July 19, 2026 |title=How fresh Messi-Yamal image signals changing of the guard |url=https://www.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/worldcup/canadamexicousa2026/articles/how-fresh-messi-yamal-image-signals-changing-of-the-guard |work=[[FIFA]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260721003339/https://www.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/worldcup/canadamexicousa2026/articles/how-fresh-messi-yamal-image-signals-changing-of-the-guard|archive-date=July 21, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=McNulty |first=Phil |date=July 20, 2026 |title=Lamine Yamal 'completes football' at 19 as Argentina betray Messi |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/c0m7zx38v43o |work=[[BBC News]]}}</ref> The encounter drew additional resonance from [[2007 Messi–Yamal photo shoot|a 2007 photograph]] in which Messi, then 20 years old, bathed the infant Yamal during a charity photo session while in [[FC Barcelona]], an image that had attracted renewed media attention in the context of their meeting on the pitch nearly two decades later.<ref name="2007photo" />

Spain's [[Ferran Torres]], who scored the only goal of the final, was named as the [[man of the match]].<ref name="MOTM">{{cite web |url=https://www.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/worldcup/canadamexicousa2026/articles/michelob-ultra-superior-player-of-match-winner |title=Michelob Ultra Superior Player of the Match – every winner |publisher=[[FIFA]] |date=June 29, 2026 |access-date=July 19, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260716095604/https://www.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/worldcup/canadamexicousa2026/articles/michelob-ultra-superior-player-of-match-winner |archive-date=July 16, 2026}}</ref> In the awards ceremony after the match, Spain's Rodri was named as the [[FIFA World Cup Golden Ball|Golden Ball]] winner as the best player of the tournament, while teammate [[Unai Simón]] won the [[FIFA World Cup Golden Glove|Golden Glove]] as the best goalkeeper of the World Cup. Compatriot [[Pau Cubarsí]] won the [[FIFA World Cup Young Player Award|FIFA Young Player Award]] as the best young player of the tournament. Messi won the Silver Ball as the second-best player of the tournament, while also securing the Silver Boot with eight goals in the tournament (only behind the ten of [[Kylian Mbappé]]).<ref>{{cite web |title=FIFA World Cup awards: Rodri, Cubarsi, Simon and Mbappe honoured |url=https://www.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/worldcup/canadamexicousa2026/articles/award-winners |publisher=[[FIFA]] |date=July 19, 2026}}</ref>

FIFA president [[Gianni Infantino]] and US president Donald Trump presented the trophy to captain [[Rodri (footballer, born 1996)|Rodri]]; both Infantino and Trump were booed by many of the fans in attendance.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Bushnell |first=Henry |date=July 19, 2026 |title=Trump booed by World Cup final crowd, takes part in trophy presentation |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/7455328/2026/07/19/trump-booed-world-cup-final/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260720005147/https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/7455328/2026/07/19/trump-booed-world-cup-final/ |archive-date=July 20, 2026 |access-date=July 20, 2026 |work=[[The Athletic]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Abnos |first=Alexander |date=July 19, 2026 |title=Donald Trump and Gianni Infantino booed before US president attempts to crash Spain celebrations |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/jul/19/donald-trump-world-cup-final |access-date=July 19, 2026 |website=The Guardian}}</ref> Trump spoke briefly with Rodri and several other Spanish players on the podium, who appeared eager to lift the trophy, but then delayed doing so while he remained with the team.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Arnold |first=Jon |title=Donald Trump awards World Cup trophy to Spain, sticks around for celebrations |url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/soccer/worldcup/2026/07/19/donald-trump-world-cup-trophy-spain-celebrations/90977197007/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260720174342/https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/soccer/worldcup/2026/07/19/donald-trump-world-cup-trophy-spain-celebrations/90977197007/ |archive-date=July 20, 2026 |access-date=July 20, 2026 |website=[[USA Today]] |language=en-US}}</ref> Infantino attempted to lead Trump out of the way of the trophy lift, but he initially insisted on remaining alongside the players, before eventually stepping aside, positioning himself at the edge of the victory photograph.<ref>{{Cite news |date=July 19, 2026 |title=Trump intenta entorpecer la celebración de España tras ganar el Mundial |url=https://www.infobae.com/america/agencias/2026/07/20/trump-intenta-entorpecer-la-celebracion-de-espana-tras-ganar-el-mundial/ |work=[[Infobae]] |language=es}}</ref>

Spain became the first country to simultaneously win both the men's and women's World Cups, having won the latter in [[2023 FIFA Women's World Cup|2023]],<ref>{{Cite web |last=Litman |first=Laken |date=July 19, 2026 |title=How Spain's Men's And Women's National Teams Rose Above The Rest Of The World |url=https://www.foxsports.com/stories/soccer/world-cup-spain-men-women-lamine-yamal-aitana-bonmati-alexia-putellas |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260720004454/https://www.foxsports.com/stories/soccer/world-cup-spain-men-women-lamine-yamal-aitana-bonmati-alexia-putellas |archive-date=July 20, 2026 |access-date=July 20, 2026 |website=[[Fox Sports]] |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Singh |first=Abhishek |date=July 20, 2026 |title=Spain become 1st nation to simultaneously hold men's and women's FIFA World Cup titles |url=https://www.financialexpress.com/sports/spain-become-1st-nation-to-simultaneously-hold-mens-and-womens-fifa-world-cup-titles/4296756/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260720004637/https://www.financialexpress.com/sports/spain-become-1st-nation-to-simultaneously-hold-mens-and-womens-fifa-world-cup-titles/4296756/ |archive-date=July 20, 2026 |access-date=July 20, 2026 |website=[[The Financial Express (India)|The Financial Express]] |language=en}}</ref> and became the first team to win the FIFA World Cup immediately after winning the [[Football at the 2024 Summer Olympics – Men's tournament|Olympic gold medal]] since [[Italy national football team|Italy]] in [[Football at the 1936 Summer Olympics|1936]] and [[1938 FIFA World Cup|1938]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Del Manto |first=Camila |date=July 20, 2026 |title=Espanha é a 1ª seleção a conquistar os títulos Olímpico e Mundial em sequência no futebol masculino em 88 anos |url=https://www.olympics.com/pt/noticias/espanha-titulos-olimpico-mundial-em-sequencia-futebol-masculino-88-anos |work=[[Olympic Games]] |language=pt}}</ref> Argentina's Lionel Messi became the second player in history to play in a World Cup final for the third time, after [[Brazil national football team|Brazil]]'s [[Cafu]] had done so in [[2002 FIFA World Cup final|2002]].<ref>{{cite news |date=July 19, 2026 |title=Lionel Messi Becomes Second-Ever Player To Appear In 3 Men's World Cup Finals |url=https://www.foxsports.com/stories/soccer/lionel-messi-becomes-second-ever-player-appear-3-mens-world-cup-finals |work=Fox Sports |accessdate=July 19, 2026}}</ref> The final also featured eleven saves by goalkeeper Martínez, the most ever recorded in a World Cup final.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Chavkin |first=Daniel |date=July 19, 2026 |title=Most saves in a World Cup final: Where Emiliano Martinez's stellar goalkeeping vs. Spain ranks in FIFA history |url=https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/most-saves-world-cup-final-212715455.html |work=[[The Sporting News]] |via=[[Yahoo Sports]]}}</ref>

===Altercations between players===
After the match concluded, multiple altercations broke out between Argentina's and Spain's players.<ref>{{cite web |last=Heverin|first=Dane|url=https://www.foxsports.com.au/football/fifa-world-cup-final-2026-argentinas-leandro-paredes-grabs-spains-eric-garcia-by-the-throat-nahuel-molina-attacks-spanish-substitutes-punches-thrown-after-final-whistle-in-violent-scenes/news-story/5c73f68b2cf92b31b1212df3594177d7|title='Sore loser': Argentina slammed over 'disgusting' act as coach makes astonishing World Cup Final claim|work=Fox Sports|date=July 20, 2026}}</ref> Argentina's defender [[Nahuel Molina]] was seen striking Spain's captain [[Rodri (footballer, born 1996)|Rodri]] in the stomach, who was running to celebrate their team's victory. Rodri instantly turned back around to confront him, in which [[Eric García (footballer, born 2001)|Eric García]] spotted them and ran over to stop them. Shortly after, [[Leandro Paredes]] tackled García, who fell to the ground, resulting in a physical altercation. Just as he was getting up, Paredes shoved him by the throat, and shortly after, Argentina's [[coaching staff]] protected García from him. Paredes then wrestled [[Gavi (footballer)|Gavi]] to the ground, with substitute [[Thiago Almada]] getting involved as he ripped his training bib.<ref>{{cite web |last=Hughes|first=Matt|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/jul/20/argentina-players-face-bans-as-fifa-opens-investigation-into-world-cup-final-brawls|title=Argentina players face bans as Fifa opens investigation into World Cup final brawls|work=The Guardian|date=July 20, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Pinner |first=Joe |date=July 20, 2026 |title=Gangs of New Jersey: how the World Cup final descended into ugly scenes between Argentina and Spain |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/jul/20/gangs-of-new-jersey-how-the-world-cup-final-descended-into-ugly-scenes-between-argentina-and-spain |access-date=July 21, 2026 |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=England|first=Adam|url=https://people.com/world-cup-final-brawl-punches-thrown-argentina-player-grabs-spanish-opponent-by-throat-12022317|title=World Cup Final Ends in Brawl as Punches Are Thrown and Argentina Player Grabs Spanish Opponent by the Throat|work=People|date=July 20, 2026}}</ref> Simultaneously, Argentina's assistant coach [[Roberto Ayala]] grabbed Spain's [[Dani Olmo]] by the bib before punching him in the face.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://onefootball.com/en/news/video-raton-ayalas-shock-punch-on-dani-olmo-after-the-final-whistle-43162030 |title=VIDEO {{!}} Ratón Ayala's shock punch on Dani Olmo after the final whistle |work=OneFootball |date=July 20, 2026 }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Rodriguez |first=Jose Victor Escobar |date=July 20, 2026 |title=Roberto Ayala caught hitting Dani Olmo during the chaotic World Cup Final brawl |url=https://www.marca.com/en/world-cup/2026/07/20/roberto-ayala-caught-hitting-dani-olmo-during-the-chaotic-world-cup-final-brawl.html |access-date=July 21, 2026 |website=Marca |language=en-US}}</ref> Multiple media outlets reported that Paredes was shown a red card after the incident,<ref>Multiple sources:
*{{Cite web |last=Braidwood |first=Jaime |date=July 20, 2026 |title=Argentina's World Cup ends with punches and in disgrace |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/leandro-paredes-red-card-argentina-spain-world-cup-b3017827.html |access-date=July 20, 2026 |website=The Independent |language=en |archive-date=July 19, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260719230136/https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/leandro-paredes-red-card-argentina-spain-world-cup-b3017827.html |url-status=live }}
*{{Cite web |last=Vertelney |first=Seth |date=July 19, 2026 |title=Argentina's Leandro Paredes shown red card for sparking brawl after World Cup final |url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/soccer/worldcup/2026/07/19/leandro-paredes-red-card-argentina-spain-world-cup-final/90970582007/ |access-date=July 20, 2026 |website=[[USA Today]] |language=en |archive-date=July 20, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260720002314/https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/soccer/worldcup/2026/07/19/leandro-paredes-red-card-argentina-spain-world-cup-final/90970582007/ |url-status=live }}
*{{Cite web |date=July 20, 2026 |title=Paredes red card mars Spain's extra time World Cup win over Argentina |url=https://www.foxnews.com/sports/world-cup-brawl-argentina-player-putting-hand-throat-spain-opponent-after-match |access-date=July 20, 2026 |website=[[Fox News]] |language=en |archive-date=July 20, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260720172828/https://www.foxnews.com/sports/world-cup-brawl-argentina-player-putting-hand-throat-spain-opponent-after-match |url-status=live }}
*{{Cite web |date=July 20, 2026 |title=Argentina's Leandro Paredes Received Red Card for What He Did After World Cup Final |url=https://www.newsweek.com/sports/argentina-player-received-red-card-for-what-he-did-after-world-cup-final-12217991 |access-date=July 20, 2026 |website=[[Newsweek]] |language=en }}</ref> but the red card did not appear in FIFA's official match report results.<ref group="Report" name="Final"/>

The actions of the Argentinian side after the end of the match were described as a "disgrace to football" by several international media outlets.<ref>Multiple sources:
*{{Cite news |last=Crafton |first=Adam |date=July 20, 2026 |title=Argentina disgraced themselves, and the World Cup final, with their charmless petulance |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/7456935/2026/07/19/argentina-world-cup-fouls-disgrace/ |access-date=July 20, 2026 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331 |archive-date=July 20, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260720023012/https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/7456935/2026/07/19/argentina-world-cup-fouls-disgrace/ |url-status=live }}
*{{Cite web |last=Heverin |first=Dane |date=July 20, 2026 |title='Disgrace': Image exposes Argentina's final classless act as coach makes WILD claim |url=https://www.foxsports.com.au/football/fifa-world-cup-final-2026-argentinas-leandro-paredes-grabs-spains-eric-garcia-by-the-throat-nahuel-molina-attacks-spanish-substitutes-punches-thrown-after-final-whistle-in-violent-scenes/news-story/5c73f68b2cf92b31b1212df3594177d7 |access-date=July 20, 2026 |website=Fox Sports |language=en }}
*{{Cite web |last=Kulawik |first=François |date=July 20, 2026 |title=Coupe du monde 2026: 'Honteux', le comportement abject des Argentins après leur défaite |url=https://www.sports.fr/football/coupe-du-monde-2026/honteux-le-comportement-abject-des-argentins-apres-leur-defaite-1030369.html |access-date=July 20, 2026 |website=Sports.fr |language=fr-FR }}</ref> Paredes was criticized for his violent behavior during and after the match,<ref>Multiple sources:
