*{{Cite news |last=Kay |first=Oliver |date=July 20, 2026 |title=Spain are worthy World Cup winners. It's a victory for method over madness |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/7457604/2026/07/20/spain-world-cup-champions-de-la-fuente/ |access-date=July 20, 2026 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331 |archive-date=July 20, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260720074154/https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/7457604/2026/07/20/spain-world-cup-champions-de-la-fuente/ |url-status=live }}
*{{Cite web |title=Mondial-2026: la victoire de l'Espagne sur l'Argentine, 'le triomphe du football' |url=https://www.trtfrancais.com/article/f69df20bb29d |access-date=July 20, 2026 |website=TRT Français |language=fr |date=July 20, 2026 }}</ref> FIFA announced an investigation in the behavior of the Argentinian players and staff, including Paredes, Molina and Ayala.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Hughes |first=Matt |date=July 20, 2026 |title=Argentina players face bans as Fifa opens investigation into World Cup final brawls |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/jul/20/argentina-players-face-bans-as-fifa-opens-investigation-into-world-cup-final-brawls |access-date=July 21, 2026 |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=FIFA opens investigation into Argentina over post-World Cup final incidents |url=https://www.euronews.com/2026/07/21/fifa-opens-investigation-into-argentina-over-post-world-cup-final-incidents |access-date=July 21, 2026 |website=Euronews}}</ref> In the days that followed the teams toned the scuffle down, with Ayala apologizing and Gavi speaking against possible suspensions for his rivals.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/c24m7prpq29o|title=Paredes should not be suspended - Spain's Gavi}}</ref>

===Aftermath and reactions===
The referee's decision to rule out Williams' goal in the 96th minute, stemming from a foul by Merino who stepped on Otamendi's foot during the build-up,<ref name="1.a.1">{{Cite web |title=Why didn't Spain goal count vs. Argentina? Explaining World Cup final call|url=https://eu.usatoday.com/story/sports/soccer/worldcup/2026/07/19/spain-goal-vs-argentina-disallowed-in-world-cup-final-nico-williams/90970591007/ |access-date=July 21, 2026 |website=[[USA Today]]|language=en}}</ref> provoked mixed reactions. Several fans and players noted that the contact was minor and of a nature that referees sometimes overlook in the penalty area,<ref>{{Cite news |last=Cons |first=Roddy |date=July 19, 2026 |title=Nico Williams goal disallowed in Spain vs Argentina World Cup final: Why was it ruled out? |url=https://en.as.com/soccer/world-cup/nico-williams-goal-disallowed-in-spain-vs-argentina-world-cup-final-why-was-it-ruled-out-f202607-n/ |work=[[Diario AS]]}}</ref><ref name="1.a.3">{{Cite web |title=Spain left 'perplexed' and 'bemused' after disallowed goal: 'It's a clear and obvious error'|url=https://football360.com.au/spain-argentina-fifa-world-cup-final-disallowed-goal-why-details-reaction/|access-date=July 21, 2026 |website=Football360|language=en}}</ref><ref name="1.a.4">{{Cite web |title=Spain fans rage after VAR chalks off Nico Williams' World Cup final goal|url=https://www.indiatoday.in/sports/football/story/world-cup-final-nico-williams-var-controversy-mikel-merino-nicolas-otamendi-2951624-2026-07-20|access-date=July 21, 2026 |website=[[India Today]]|language=en}}</ref> and highlighted that Otamendi had his arm around Merino prior to the incident.<ref name="1.a.2">{{Cite web |title=Should Nico's goal have stood?: VAR, Argentina and the questions that won't go away|url=https://www.thedailystar.net/sports/sports-special/fifa-world-cup-2026/news/should-nicos-goal-have-stood-var-argentina-and-the-questions-wont-go-away-4228106|access-date=July 21, 2026 |website=[[The Daily Star (Bangladesh)|The Daily Star]]|language=en}}</ref> During the match, Spain supporters sarcastically chanted "Infantino" following the disallowed goal, referencing allegations of FIFA favoring Argentina.<ref name="1.a.3" />

Celebrations broke out among supporters across various parts of Spain.<ref>{{Cite news |date=July 19, 2026 |title=Las celebraciones de España tras ganar su segundo Mundial, en imágenes |url=https://elpais.com/deportes/2026-07-20/las-celebraciones-de-espana-tras-ganar-su-segundo-mundial-en-imagenes.html |work=[[El País]] |language=es}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Lyons |first=Emmet |date=July 20, 2026 |title=Spain rejoices in World Cup victory, even if some fans say Trump lingered too long in team's photo-op |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/spain-world-cup-2026-fans-trump-photo/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260720174342/https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/soccer/worldcup/2026/07/19/donald-trump-world-cup-trophy-spain-celebrations/90977197007/ |archive-date=July 20, 2026 |access-date=July 20, 2026 |website=[[CBS News]] |language=en-US}}</ref> In [[Ciudad Rodrigo|Ciudad Rodrigo, Salamanca]], a 13-year-old died and three others were injured when the fountain at the Glorieta del Árbol Gordo collapsed over them.<ref>{{Cite news |date=July 20, 2026 |title=Muere un adolescente tras el derrumbe de una fuente en Ciudad Rodrigo en las celebraciones del Mundial |url=https://www.elconfidencial.com/espana/castilla-y-leon/2026-07-20/derrumbe-fuente-ciudad-rodrigo-1tna-1tps_4392637/ |work=[[El Confidencial]] |language=es}}</ref> A 20-year-old also died in [[Sonseca]] during what was reported as a convulsion. Across Spain that evening, more than 80 people were reported injured and approximately 12 arrested.<ref>{{Cite news |date=July 20, 2026 |title=Celebraciones nocturnas por victoria de España dejan dos muertos y más de 80 heridos |url=https://www.jornada.com.mx/noticia/2026/07/20/mundial/dos-muertos-y-mas-de-80-heridos-tras-festejos-por-triunfo-de-espana-en-el-mundial |work=[[La Jornada]] |language=es}}</ref> In New York City, celebrations broke out in several parts of the city, including [[Times Square]], [[Central Park]], and [[Little Spain, Manhattan]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Dhaliwal |first=Naveen |last2=Kliger |first2=Hannah |last3=Ramos |first3=Andrew |date=July 19, 2026 |title=Fans who couldn't score tickets to World Cup final in N.J. head to NYC watch parties |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/newyork/news/nyc-world-cup-fan-reaction-watch-parties/ |work=[[CBS News]]}}</ref> In [[Mexico City]], where there is a large Spaniard community, several Spain supporters and Mexico national team fans celebrated at the [[Fuente de Cibeles (Mexico City)|Fountain of Cybele]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=George |first=Israel |date=July 29, 2026 |title=Españoles en CdMx celebran triunfo de España en la Copa Mundial 2026 |url=https://www.milenio.com/comunidad/fiesta-en-el-angel-de-la-independencia-por-final-de-mundial-2026 |work=La Afición |publisher=[[Milenio]] |language=Spanish|url-access=limited}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Méndez |first=Arturo |date=July 19, 2026 |title=Festejaron en la capital: Miles de aficionados se reunieron en la Cibeles de la CDMX para celebrar el campeonato del mundo |url=https://oem.com.mx/esto/mundial-2026/aficionados-espanoles-festejaron-en-la-cibeles-de-la-cdmx-31207112 |url-access=limited |work=ESTO |publisher=[[Organización Editorial Mexicana]] |language=es}}</ref>

In [[Buenos Aires]], fans and government officials gathered at [[Ezeiza International Airport]] to receive the national team, where the [[Armed Forces of the Argentine Republic|Argentine Armed Forces]] performed an orchestra rendition of the football chant ''{{ill|Muchachos, ahora nos volvimos a ilusionar|lt=|es|Muchachos, ahora nos volvimos a ilusionar}}'' ({{Translation|Guys, we have our hopes up again}}) and a [[Drone art|drone show]] marked their arrival.<ref>{{Cite news |date=20 July 2026 |title=La selección argentina llegó al país tras la final del Mundial: parte del plantel recibió el saludo de una multitud en Ezeiza |url=https://www.a24.com/deportes/la-seleccion-argentina-regresa-al-pais-y-los-hinchas-esperan-al-plantel-el-predio-la-afa-n1577048 |work=[[América 24]] |language=Spanish|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260721134917/https://www.a24.com/deportes/la-seleccion-argentina-regresa-al-pais-y-los-hinchas-esperan-al-plantel-el-predio-la-afa-n1577048|archive-date=21 July 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> Messi and several other players did not travel to Buenos Aires, instead flying directly to their club destinations or to begin their holidays. The arriving players were transported through the city on an open-top bus, greeted by large crowds and fireworks along the route.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Rodríguez |first=Irene |date=21 July 2026 |title=Argentina recibe a la selección con una fiesta tras perder la final del Mundial ante España, sin Leo Messi |url=https://www.antena3.com/noticias/deportes/futbol/argentina-recibe-seleccion-fiesta-obelisco-perder-final-mundial-espana-leo-messi_202607216a5f180e303ca6202cc2ceaf.html |work=Antena 3 |language=Spanish|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260722143444/https://www.antena3.com/noticias/deportes/futbol/argentina-recibe-seleccion-fiesta-obelisco-perder-final-mundial-espana-leo-messi_202607216a5f180e303ca6202cc2ceaf.html|archive-date=22 July 2026|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Preve |first=Clara |last2=Debre |first2=Isabel |date=July 20, 2026 |title=Argentinos salen a las calles para homenajear a selección pese a derrota en final del Mundial |url=https://www.latimes.com/espanol/deportes/articulo/2026-07-20/argentinos-salen-las-calles-para-homenajear-seleccion-pese-derrota-en-final-del-mundial |work=[[Los Angeles Times]] |language=Spanish}}</ref> Thousands of additional supporters gathered at the [[Obelisco de Buenos Aires|Obelisk]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=19 July 2026 |title=Miles de hinchas se juntaron en el Obelisco para apoyar a la Selección Argentina tras la final del Mundial |url=https://radiomitre.cienradios.com/deportes/miles-de-hinchas-se-juntaron-en-el-obelisco-para-apoyar-a-la-seleccion-argentina-tras-la-final-del-mundial/ |work=[[Radio Mitre]] |language=Spanish}}</ref> The celebrations were marred by riots in which supporters threw stones, glass bottles, and other objects at police.<ref>{{Cite news|title=Fans riot in Argentina after World Cup defeat to Spain|url= https://www.belfastlive.co.uk/news/uk-world-news/fans-riot-argentina-after-world-34317943|work=Belfast Live|date=July 20, 2026|last1=Cailer|first1=Adam|last2=Care|first2=Adam|last3=Davies|first3=Ethan|access-date=July 20, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|title=Argentina fans throw stones at police in Buenos Aires after World Cup final loss|url=https://www.channelnewsasia.com/shorts/argentina-fans-throw-stones-police-in-buenos-aires-after-world-cup-final-loss-6265211|work=Channel News Asia|access-date=July 20, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|title=Argentina fans hurl rocks at riot police after World Cup defeat|url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/world-news/2026/07/20/argentina-fans-throw-rocks-police-world-cup-buenos-aires/|work=The Daily Telegraph|date=July 20, 2026|last=Smith|first=Emily|access-date=July 20, 2026}}</ref> Riot police responded with water cannons, tear gas, and rubber bullets to disperse the crowds. Local police reported at least fifteen arrests and several injuries during the clashes.<ref>{{Cite news|date=July 20, 2026|title=Without Messi, Argentine team set for low-key homecoming|url=https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20260720-without-messi-argentine-team-set-for-low-key-homecoming|work=France24|access-date=July 20, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|date=July 20, 2026|title=Argentina fans clash with police in Buenos Aires after World Cup final defeat|url=https://www.tbsnews.net/world/argentina-fans-clash-police-buenos-aires-after-world-cup-final-defeat-1492921|work=[[The Business Standard]]|access-date=July 21, 2026}}</ref>

The Spain national team returned to Madrid the next day and was welcomed at the [[Madrid–Barajas Airport]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Naishadham |first=Suman |date=July 20, 2026 |title=Spain's World Cup champions return home for royal welcome and parade through Madrid |url=https://apnews.com/article/spain-fifa-world-cup-champions-team-cd1705a614f6ffd79da5e217f63faaaa |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260720175301/https://apnews.com/article/spain-fifa-world-cup-champions-team-cd1705a614f6ffd79da5e217f63faaaa |archive-date=July 20, 2026 |access-date=July 20, 2026 |website=[[AP News]] |language=en}}</ref> The World Cup victory parade happened at 7:00&nbsp;pm [[Central European Summer Time|CEST]] ([[UTC+02:00|UTC+2]]) through central Madrid, where the attendance was expected to be over a million,<ref>{{Cite news |last=Jones |first=Sam |date=July 20, 2026 |title=More than a million people expected at Spain's World Cup celebration in Madrid |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/jul/20/spain-world-cup-celebration-madrid |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260720175655/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/jul/20/spain-world-cup-celebration-madrid |archive-date=July 20, 2026 |access-date=July 20, 2026 |work=[[The Guardian]] |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |agency=Agence France-Presse |date=July 20, 2026 |title=Spain's World Cup heroes return home ahead of victory parade |url=https://courthousenews.com/spains-world-cup-heroes-return-home-ahead-of-victory-parade |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260720175523/https://courthousenews.com/spains-world-cup-heroes-return-home-ahead-of-victory-parade/ |archive-date=July 20, 2026 |access-date=July 20, 2026 |website=[[Courthouse News Service]] |language=en-us}}</ref> although the number ended up being closer to two million.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Dos millones de personas reciben a la selección de España |url=https://www.dw.com/es/dos-millones-de-personas-reciben-a-la-selecci%C3%B3n-de-espa%C3%B1a-en-madrid/a-78042665 |access-date=July 21, 2026 |website=Deutsche Welle |language=es}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Gosende |first=Ana |last2=Vicedo |first2=Paula |date=July 20, 2026 |title=Dos millones de personas inundan las calles de Madrid: 'En 2030 la Copa volverá a ser nuestra' |url=https://www.elmundo.es/deportes/2026/07/21/6a5e9d0ae9cf4ac0438b4597.html |access-date=July 21, 2026 |website=El Mundo |language=es|url-access=subscription}}</ref> The parade concluded at [[Plaza de Cibeles]], where the Spanish team did a trophy lift in front of a large crowd.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Pérez Díaz |first=Aaron |last2=La Casa |first2=Rafa |date=July 21, 2026 |title=Dos millones de personas honraron a los reyes del mundo: la Selección desborda Madrid en el recibimiento a los héroes |url=https://www.elconfidencial.com/deportes/futbol/mundial/2026-07-21/espana-celebracion-fiesta-rua-campeones-mundo_4393195/ |work=[[El Confidencial]] |language=Spanish}}</ref>

